  "step_3": "The decision reason requires computing an aspiration level as the mean of all outcomes (ignoring probabilities) and then evaluating each lottery based on the probability of exceeding this level. The aspiration level (-1750) and the resulting positive differences (+1750 for 0 in both lotteries) are not mentioned or implied in the verbal report. The individual does not refer to any such reference point or comparison of outcomes relative to a computed average. Instead, the justification centers on minimizing the worst possible loss ('weniger Verlust'), which reflects a minimax or loss-aversion heuristic, not the aspiration-level rule described. While both lotteries have the same positive outcome (0), and the individual pays attention to both outcomes and probabilities, there is no indication that they computed or used a mean outcome as a reference. The reasoning is more aligned with focusing on the worst outcome and trying to avoid the larger loss. Therefore, the information relevant to the decision reason (aspiration level and positive deviations) was not considered, and the justification does not align with the rule of preferring the lottery with higher probability of positive differences from the aspiration level.",
